invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser.c
catches: srv_test
reason: the extension loop's default arm refuses an extension it does not
  recognize, the client's habit, where RFC 9846 §4.2.2 makes a server
  ignore it (rfc9846.txt:1299) and §9.3 restates that as a protocol
  invariant (rfc9846.txt:4636-4637). A hello carrying a GREASE extension
  would then never negotiate, and every browser sends one. The golden
  hello in test/srv_parser_tests.h carries an unknown type and must
  parse.

--- old
    if (!srv_ext_known(type)) {
        return CH_OK;
    }
--- new
    if (!srv_ext_known(type)) {
        return srv_refuse(p->alert, ALERT_UNSUPPORTED_EXTENSION);
    }
